        mc2:ToolOutputFormatEnum ;
    skos:definition "An HDF5 file appears to the user as a directed graph whose nodes are higher-level HDF5 objects, such as groups, datasets, and named datatypes, used to store and organize large amounts of numerical and hierarchical data.",
        "H5AD is an HDF5-based file format used by the AnnData Python library (and Scanpy/Seurat-compatible tools) to store annotated data matrices, such as single-cell gene-expression counts, together with associated observation and variable (cell/gene) metadata.",
        "HDF5, the current version of the Hierarchical Data Format; a data model, library, and file format for storing and managing large, complex, heterogeneous data." .

